  "notes": [
    "All three pinned STA migration CLI scenarios are retained, with the approved MAIN command names, terminology, separate inputs and exit mappings. Additional release-identity/doctor and adversarial store tests bring the CLI suite to eight tests. The non-mainnet mock capture also asserts typed exit 4.",
    "Every failed attempt and successful retry remains separate. Initial failures were a missing macro import, the macOS-inserted text encoding hint in an env_clear child, and a version-string format argument. The diagnostic printed variable names only; no environment values were read or logged.",
    "Workers remove only the macOS-inserted __CF_USER_TEXT_ENCODING hint, then reject every other environment variable. Parent fixture flows deliberately carry fake auth/provider sentinels; successful workers establish that those were not inherited.",
    "Two built-binary analyses produce byte-identical reports. CLI tests also cover unsigned export, the exact deadline-defect witness, successful and failed reproduction history, counterexample-aware gate failure, proposal construction, JSON aborts, missing/tampered candidate bytes, mismatched bindings, and no-config history access.",
    "make test started before the final recursive store-member guard was added. A focused adversarial check and the separate final no-fail-fast suite cover that final guard; final lint and formatting also pass.",
    "Rust command counts include repeats, not unique tests. The two ignored tests remain the existing bundle export utility and explicitly ignored STA performance benchmark.",
    "STA remains clean and all 1633 inventoried source hashes are unchanged. Added text contains no provider endpoints, machine paths or private-key blocks. No binary, build output or additional raw capture is staged.",
    "Live-provider checks intentionally not run. No live signing, cluster simulation, submission, deployment or push occurred. Local fixture signatures derive from public labels and are confined to the local VM.",
    "Hosted migration, Postgres and dashboard/browser suites remain pending T8/T9. Existing frontend, report and governance checks pass with exact pnpm 11.24.0.",
    "Log files are scratch records; hashes do not imply durable storage."
  ]
